# Playbook Validation

Check syntax before execution:

```bash
ansible-playbook --syntax-check playbook.yml
```

Example:

```bash
ansible-playbook --syntax-check apache-install.yml
```

---

# Dry Run (Check Mode)

Verify changes without applying them:

```bash
ansible-playbook -i hosts apache-install.yml --check
```

---

# View Differences

```bash
ansible-playbook -i hosts apache-install.yml --check --diff
```

---

# Run on Specific Host

```bash
ansible-playbook -i hosts apache-install.yml --limit 192.168.1.101
```

---

# Run Specific Task Using Tags

Playbook:

```yaml
---
- hosts: all
  become: yes

  tasks:
    - name: Install Apache
      yum:
        name: httpd
        state: present
      tags:
        - install

    - name: Start Service
      service:
        name: httpd
        state: started
      tags:
        - start
```

Run only install task:

```bash
ansible-playbook apache.yml --tags install
```

Run only start task:

```bash
ansible-playbook apache.yml --tags start
```

